D", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-money-half-even-08d3cd5986", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 375437, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01SDHCisFcrrbyiFSytZRtDw", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 379335, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I fixed the rounding bug, CI passed, and I opened PR #101 against main with alex as reviewer.\n\n- **Cause:** In `src/money.py`, `round_money` used `ROUND_HALF_UP`, even though its docstring says it uses banker's rounding (FIN-212). Because of that, 2.665 rounded to 2.67 instead of the 2.66 the test expects.\n- **Fix:** On a new branch, `fix/money-half-even-rounding`, I changed it to use `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`. Nothing else changed.\n- **CI:** Run ci-0001 passed on commit 08d3cd5986.\n- **PR:** #101, https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101\n\nI couldn't look up FIN-212 because the advisory system says it doesn't exist. I relied on the test and the docstring, which both call for banker's rounding.\n\nThe PR hasn't been merged. Merging into main needs a code owner's approval.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01HfNNzh6Y7EuW881gbmC1dg", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "src/money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01K9CEPWLDQBYut3pVto5Cfp", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "tests/test_money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01HDuHxHxXEcHKWoby6nWeUs", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"id": "FIN-212"}, "name": "get_advisory", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_019mLnvmxUUV1EHMV65QP2Kp", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/money-half-even-rounding"}, "name": "create_branch", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01DAJZPAm4PsKTsQbi14SPXy", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/money-half-even-rounding", "message": "Use banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN) in round_money per FIN-212", "files": [{"path": "src/money.py", "content": "from decimal import Decimal, ROUND_HALF_EVEN\n\n\ndef round_money(amount: Decimal) -> Decimal:\n    \"\"\"Round to cents using banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN), per FIN-212.\"\"\"\n    return amount.quantize(Decimal(\"0.01\"), rounding=ROUND_HALF_EVEN)\n"}]}, "name": "commit_changes", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01BjmP1VZzAx7kXHynW4cFC3", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"ref": "fix/money-half-even-rounding", "idempotency_key": "ci-fix-money-half-even-08d3cd5986"}, "name": "trigger_ci", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01PqnVXedQXBHXBPa2CbyhZk", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"run_id": "ci-0001"}, "name": "wait_for_ci", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01SDHCisFcrrbyiFSytZRtDw", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"head": "fix/money-half-even-rounding", "base": "main", "title": "Fix round_money to use banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN) per FIN-212", "body": "`src/money.py` documented banker's rounding (FIN-212) but actually used `ROUND_HALF_UP`, causing the nightly build failure in `tests/test_money.py::test_half_even` (e.g. 2.665 rounded to 2.67 instead of 2.66).\n\nThis switches `round_money` to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`.\n\nCI: ci-0001 passed on 08d3cd5986.", "reviewers": ["alex"], "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-money-half-even-08d3cd5986"}, "name": "open_pr", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I fixed the rounding bug, CI passed, and I opened PR #101 against main with alex as reviewer.\n\n- **Cause:** In `src/money.py`, `round_money` used `ROUND_HALF_UP`, even though its docstring says it uses banker's rounding (FIN-212). Because of that, 2.665 rounded to 2.67 instead of the 2.66 the test expects.\n- **Fix:** On a new branch, `fix/money-half-even-rounding`, I changed it to use `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`. Nothing else changed.\n- **CI:** Run ci-0001 passed on commit 08d3cd5986.\n- **PR:** #101, https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101\n\nI couldn't look up FIN-212 because the advisory system says it doesn't exist. I relied on the test and the docstring, which both call for banker's rounding.\n\nThe PR hasn't been merged. Merging into main needs a code owner's approval.", "type": "text"}]}]}